{
  "info": {
    "name": "Decidiq Implementation Progress Reminder Suite",
    "description": "Newman test for change followup-implementation-progress task 5 (REQ-FUP-004): the declared scheduled rule `implementationSilent` on the decision schema tells the secretariat when an adopted decision has had no progress update for 90 days. It seeds three adopted motions: one decided 100 days ago with no update (reported), one with an update 10 days ago and one reported completed (both not reported). It switches background jobs to webcron, calls cron.php until OpenRegister's ScheduledNotificationJob has run (at most 150 calls), reads the secretary's notifications and restores the background job mode. The rule fires at most once a day per instance (intervalSec 86400), so run it on a fresh instance, as the nightly does. Written, not yet run: it needs a live instance. It is the unattended, single-pass form of tests/newman/implementation-progress.json, which needs a docker exec cron.php between two passes; this one sits in tests/integration so the CI Newman job runs it.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
